{"status": "ok", "comment": "Fixed the precedence bug in conf/settings.py by reordering the lookup logic so environment variables (APP_*) override the built-in DEFAULTS, matching the runbook and tests.", "file_path": "conf/settings.py", "content": """"Runtime settings.

Precedence (documented in the ops runbook): an environment variable always
overrides the built-in default. Variables are prefixed APP_ and upper-cased.
"""

import os

DEFAULTS = {"timeout": 30, "retries": 3, "verbose": "0"}


def get(key: str) -> str:
    if os.environ.get("APP_" + key.upper()) is not None:
        return os.environ["APP_" + key.upper()]
    if key in DEFAULTS:
        return DEFAULTS[key]
    return ""
